From f7339a3fb96bc76bb52687e0242c01c69ff3d3ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Juta <ericjohnjuta@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:13:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] atelet: run actors from Nix store paths

A container or image volume reference of the form nix:/nix/store/<hash>-<name>
is served from the node's Nix store instead of an OCI registry. atelet asks
the Nix daemon to substitute the closure, hard-links it into a per-closure
view and hands that view to the worker through the existing overlay spec, so
no image is built, pushed or pulled.

When the daemon will not take the closure, the error starts with the reason:
no configured cache has the path, a cache has it unsigned, or a cache has it
signed only by keys the node does not trust, named from the cache's narinfo.
nix-store's stderr tells a missing path from a refused one but not an
unsigned path from an untrusted signature, so atelet reads the refused
path's narinfo from the http(s) cache, bounded in time and size, and falls
back to nix-store's error when it cannot.

Nix prints a substituter URL's user name and password verbatim. Every
nix-store error atelet returns has the userinfo and query of each URL
redacted.
