diff --git a/docs/guides/nix-images.md b/docs/guides/nix-images.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..70f6aeac
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/guides/nix-images.md
@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+---
+title: "Nix Images"
+linkTitle: "Nix Images"
+weight: 30
+description: >
+  Run actors from Nix store paths instead of OCI images: no registry, no layers, no per-run pulls.
+---
+
+# Nix images
+
+A container's `image` normally names an OCI image pinned by digest. On nodes
+that run a Nix daemon it can name a Nix store path instead:
+
+```yaml
+containers:
+- name: agent
+  image: nix:/nix/store/0c0zb1l7mqvdrsgjq7b9vl0g9cyfh3q1-agent-env
+```
+
+The store path is the root of a closure that was built and signed ahead of
+time, by CI or a sandboxed builder. The node never evaluates or builds Nix
+code. When an actor starts, atelet asks the node's Nix daemon to substitute
+the paths of the closure that the node does not yet have, then exposes exactly
+that closure to the actor as its root filesystem.
+
+What this changes compared with an OCI image:
+
+- **Unit of delivery.** One store path per package rather than one layer per
+  build step. A change ships the changed derivations and their dependents,
+  nothing else.
+- **No per-run pull.** A node fetches only the paths it lacks, in parallel,
+  from its own store first and then from its binary caches. There is no unpack
+  step.
+- **Sharing is per package.** Two templates that both contain `nodejs` use the
+  same files on disk and the same page cache.
+- **No registry in the critical path.** A node that already has the closure
+  starts actors with every cache unreachable.
+- **Supply chain.** The daemon accepts only paths signed by a key the node
+  trusts. The reference is content-addressed, so it is pinned by construction.
+
+Image volumes accept the same reference form.
+
+## What the actor sees
+
+The actor's root filesystem is a read-only view of the closure, under the
+actor's usual private writable layer:
+
+- `/nix/store/<path>` for every path in the closure, and no other path from
+  the node's store.
+- For each top-level directory of the root path (`bin`, `etc`, `lib`, ...), a
+  directory of the same name whose entries link into the root path. A root
+  built with `pkgs.buildEnv` therefore gives the actor `/bin/sh`,
+  `/etc/passwd` and so on.
+- Empty `/proc`, `/sys`, `/dev`, `/tmp` and `/etc` where the root path does
+  not provide them.
+
+The store is read-only inside the actor. Writes go to the actor's private
+layer and are snapshotted as with any image.
+
+### Image config
+
+An OCI image carries its entrypoint, environment, working directory and user
+in its config. A Nix image carries the same fields, in the same JSON shape, in
+an optional file named `ate-image-config.json` at the top of the root path:
+
+```nix
+pkgs.buildEnv {
+  name = "agent-env";
+  paths = [
+    pkgs.bashInteractive pkgs.coreutils pkgs.ripgrep
+    (pkgs.writeTextDir "ate-image-config.json" (builtins.toJSON {
+      Entrypoint = [ "/bin/bash" ];
+      Env = [ "PATH=/bin" ];
+      WorkingDir = "/work";
+    }))
+  ];
+}
+```
+
+The template's `command`, `args` and `env` override it exactly as they
+override an OCI image's config. Without the file, the template must set
+`command`.
+
+## Node setup
+
+Nix images need three things on every node that runs them.
+
+1. **A Nix daemon** whose `nix.conf` lists your binary caches as
+   `substituters` and your signing keys as `trusted-public-keys`, with
+   `require-sigs` left on. This is where the trust policy lives; atelet passes
+   no substituter or key of its own.
+
+2. **atelet with access to the store.** Mount the host's `/nix` into the
+   atelet container and set:
+
+   | Flag | Value |
+   |---|---|
+   | `--nix-view-dir` | A directory on the same mount as `/nix/store`, for example `/nix/var/ate/views`. Setting it enables Nix images. |
+   | `--nix-store-command` | The `nix-store` executable, for example `/nix/var/nix/profiles/system/sw/bin/nix-store` on NixOS. |
+   | `--nix-view-mount-dir` | The path at which worker pods see the view directory, if different. See below. |
+
+   atelet builds each view out of hard links, which is why the view directory
+   must share a mount with the store. atelet talks to the daemon over its
+   socket under `/nix/var/nix/daemon-socket` and never writes the store.
+
+3. **Worker pods that can see the views.** Workers mount only `/var/lib/ate`
+   from the host. Bind-mount the view directory beneath it on the node and
+   tell atelet where it appears:
+
+   ```nix
+   fileSystems."/var/lib/ate/nix-views" = {
+     device = "/nix/var/ate/views";
+     options = [ "bind" ];
+   };
+   ```
+
+   ```
+   --nix-view-dir=/nix/var/ate/views
+   --nix-view-mount-dir=/var/lib/ate/nix-views
+   ```
+
+A template that names a Nix image on a node where `--nix-view-dir` is unset
+fails to start with an error saying so. Use a worker pool's node selector to
+keep such templates on Nix nodes.
+
+## When a node refuses an image
+
+If the node's daemon cannot substitute the closure, the template's golden
+snapshot fails with `GoldenActorCrashed`, and atelet's message starts with
+the reason:
+
+| Message starts with | Cause |
+|---|---|
+| `no binary cache configured on this node has /nix/store/...` | No cache in the daemon's `substituters` has the path. Push the closure to one. |
+| `no binary cache this node could reach has /nix/store/...` | The same, but at least one cache did not answer; nix-store's warnings follow. |
+| `binary cache <url> has /nix/store/..., but it carries no signature` | The cache has the path unsigned. Sign it (`nix store sign`) with a key in the node's `trusted-public-keys`. |
+| `binary cache <url> has /nix/store/..., signed only by keys this node does not trust: <names>` | The path is signed, but by none of the node's `trusted-public-keys`. The names are the key names from the cache's narinfo. |
+
+Nix itself only reports that a cache's copy is "not signed by any of the keys
+in 'trusted-public-keys'". To tell an unsigned path from one signed by an
+unknown key, atelet reads that path's narinfo from the cache, for `http` and
+`https` caches, within one 5-second budget and 64 KiB per narinfo. It never
+asks the daemon to take the path. nix-store's own error follows the reason;
+when atelet cannot read the narinfo or does not recognise nix-store's output,
+the message is nix-store's error alone. In every message the user name,
+password and query of a cache URL are shown as `[redacted]`.
+
+## Garbage collection
+
+Each view registers a Nix GC root for its closure, so the Nix collector never
+removes a closure that a view on the node still stands for. atelet removes a
+view, and its root, once no actor bundle on the node references it and it has
+been unused for `--image-cache-min-age`; the pass runs every
+`--image-cache-gc-period`. After that the node's ordinary `nix-collect-garbage`
+schedule reclaims the paths.
+
+A suspended actor does not keep a view on the node: its closure is refetched
+from the binary cache when it resumes. Keep every closure that a live or
+suspended actor references in your binary cache.
